+/*
+ * How long an encode job may stay in flight before the driver stops waiting for the firmware.
+ *
+ * The firmware reports its own watchdog (WAVE5_SYSERR_WATCHDOG_TIMEOUT) about 125 ms after a
+ * picture it cannot finish, and that report arrives as an ordinary completion which
+ * finish_encode already handles. The default sits well above that, so it fires only when no
+ * completion arrives at all. That case has nothing else to break it: v4l2_m2m_cancel_job() waits
+ * uninterruptibly with no timeout, holding the mutex both video nodes are registered with, so one
+ * unanswered job takes the encoder and both decoders down until the SoC is power cycled.
+ *
